  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Thursday)\nIssued at 1217 AM CDT Fri Sep 18 2026\n\nActive weather looks to hold for the long term period as present\nmodel agreement sees the upper-level trough continue its path into\nthe Northern Great Plains Sunday. This push will help to\nreinvigorate linger boundaries still in the Panhandles and allow\nus another crack at the monsoonal moisture. Currently, our best\nchances are holding across the Northern and Eastern Panhandles for\nthe day, but do begin to spread further west as we head into the\novernight and early Monday. By that afternoon, present models do\nsee a new disturbance follow that could lead to another round of\nstorms across the Southern and Central Panhandles. However, the\nbetter chance may be on Tuesday as models see a yet another trough\npush in from Southern California and force the upper-level high\nwell south into Central Mexico. From here model agreement gets a\nlittle muddy as runs try to keep the active pattern going with a\ncombination of short-wave disturbances and potential weak frontal\nboundaries pushing in from our north. Regardless, the combination\nof this active pattern as well as the retreat of the high into\nMexico will see much cooler temperatures across the Panhandles. As\nit stands, look for highs to be in the in the mid to upper 80s as\nearly as Sunday with potential to be in the mid 70s by Tuesday\nafternoon.",
